 "title": "Open ends make a substitution tower stretch",
 "subject": "When a law that grows by substituting knots can move its original distinctions apart",
 "conclusion": "A hub-free parity substitution keeps the replaced knot exactly when its gadget adds no open end, and then every step is conservative, so the original distinctions stay at bond distance 2 forever; this is why the 2026-10-20 refinement cannot grow space. On tree-shaped knot graphs bond distance equals the path's knot count plus one, so the star tower stretches as 3^k + 1.",
